body: "## Hosted exact-head evidence, not a local crash reproduction\n\nPR #150 remains at `8b945eb750300ba24eb0e32f1f37c6d2e66fe0dc`, rechecked 2026-10-27 19:18 UTC. Its [Node 26 job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/40541474002/job/122320706483) finished with 2,217 tests, 2,211 passes and six failures. Five concern native interruption or power-loss recovery:\n\n- Purge-journal/unlink boundary convergence: `unsupported_erasure_storage` from `assertSupportedControl`.\n- Native lifecycle-journal recovery: cut 645 / directory:openSync:before yields the same typed refusal.\n- Repack power boundary 3990/3990 (directory-flushed): `DestructionRefusal`, preserving replaced/unplanned entries rather than completing the expected receipt.\n- Packed-GC power boundary 3336/3336: a planned object remains where the recovery assertion expects none.\n- Obliterate power boundary 2926/2926: `unsupported_erasure_storage`.\n\nThe sixth failure is a separate exported-reader enumeration assertion. Branch coverage also remains below 100% in bisect/destruction. These failures are recorded together as current gate evidence, not attributed to a single root cause. Current Node 22 is also failed; Windows launcher jobs are green. No newer successful run superseded these checks at observation.\n\nThe [erasure guard](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/8b945eb750300ba24eb0e32f1f37c6d2e66fe0dc/engine/erasure.ts#L67-L74) correctly refuses unrecognized control entries or symlinks. The log does not identify the offending entry or establish that this guard should be weakened. The relevant matrices are [native lifecycle](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/8b945eb750300ba24eb0e32f1f37c6d2e66fe0dc/test/erasure-lifecycle.test.ts#L102) and [power-loss durability](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/8b945eb750300ba24eb0e32f1f37c6d2e66fe0dc/test/journal-durability.test.ts#L130).\n\n## Expected, actual and impact\n\nThe [canonical pm-vcs-phase6packs record](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/8b945eb750300ba24eb0e32f1f37c6d2e66fe0dc/.agents/pm/features/pm-vcs-phase6packs.toon) requires preserved logical identities, resumable publication and safe interruption/erasure compatibility.\n\nExpected: supported native crash images converge under the documented retry protocol with exact, truthful receipts. Actual: current exact-head hosted recovery matrices do not meet those assertions, blocking pack/recovery certification. Windows launcher success and focused local checks do not establish these Linux crash matrices.\n\nThis is not evidence of user-data loss, a released-artifact regression or an unsafe successful erase. Root cause, including whether a fixture or oracle is invalid, remains unproven. No local SIGKILL, destructive operation, provider mutation or implementation change was performed.\n\n## Acceptance and regression criteria\n\n- Diagnose the exact control entry, receipt ownership and state at each failing boundary using sanitized fixture evidence.\n- Make supported retries converge, or correct an evidenced invalid oracle, while retaining fail-closed behavior for foreign/replaced entries. Do not globally relax the unsupported-storage guard.\n- Preserve authoritative history and exact deletion/retirement receipts; retain reader-enumeration coverage and unchanged thresholds.\n- Rerun the existing failing matrices and complete Node 22/26 npm/Bun gates on one immutable final head. Report outcomes separately from Windows launcher and packed-consumer evidence.\n\nDeduplication: all 157 all-status issue/PR records, current PR #150 discussion/reviews and the canonical phase-six record were inspected. Existing #151 concerns annotation teardown ENOTEMPTY; #154 concerns ENOSPC cascades. Neither owns this current recovery failure class. PR #150 and pm-vcs-phase6packs remain the implementation owners.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (8)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-31T18:57:32Z)\n>\n> Retained native recovery repair: [6b6c002](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/commit/6b6c0028f777ecb55465e9a8bbfc7762caedbda5). Further erasure fixes and regression protection are in `6dfc77631fdd528761aa7331f41588de481dde52`.\n> \n> The earlier failures involved verified native process markers, original directory-retirement receipts and operation-log ownership/deduplication. The power-loss oracle also copied bytes while incorrectly changing logical mtime across namespace-only alias operations. Those repairs are retained; foreign and replaced entries still refuse.\n> \n> The independent Codex BLOCK review of f4d4cf6 found two additional defects addressed here: opaque destruction-directory contents could survive a successful receipt, and logical-ID deduplication dropped physical copies after interrupted unpack. The guard now validates exact native artifacts and pinned ref metadata, including real native zero-byte creation stages without granting authority. Preflight retains every physical location, and unpack validates intentionally denied duplicate loose copies through the existing writer-lease-scoped physical API. Ordinary reads still enforce denial.\n> \n> Six isolated behavior reversions fail and restored selections pass, including erasure_retained_copy and object_obliterated. New packed durability: 1/1; 5,546 native boundaries, 474 distinct complete crash images, two successful replays per image. Focused erasure: 103/103 across accountability, fragment repairs and storage, zero failures/skips/cancellations. Lifecycle: **42/42**, covering 35 selected native cuts across the 722/934 default matrices, a real SIGKILL after the last unpacked member, three selected physical copies, retained peer bytes and one idempotent receipt. Pack suite: **38/38**. Node 22 review selection: **10/10**. Full matrices remain enabled in CI; local filtered cuts are not whole-matrix certification. An expanded local command including the roughly 25-minute seeded model hit its 15-minute orchestration timeout after the selected cuts passed; that attempt is not a passing gate.\n> \n> [Repair report](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/6dfc77631fdd528761aa7331f41588de481dde52/docs/validation/pr150-erasure-review-repair.md). [Exact-head CI](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/41231846990) is pending, and fresh independent Codex review remains required. No closure, merge or release is performed.\n> \n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-31T20:30:24Z)\n>\n> The decoded-state repair is in [5019dade6d6f23e3017d141228461a1810ac9d4d](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/commit/5019dade6d6f23e3017d141228461a1810ac9d4d), supplementing the retained native ownership/recovery and physical-copy fixes.\n> \n> The re-review of 6dfc776 reproduced success while a quoted payload remained recoverable from an escaped destruction path. Raw serialized text was insufficient. The repair uses one bounded incremental JSON string decoder for materialized and streaming inspection, including keys, all escapes and UTF-16 pairs. Hex/base64/framing/compression compose under existing bounds, and recoverable prefixes are inspected even when a new codec guess later errors. Existing declared raw/base64 refusals, strict journal classification and physical-copy recovery remain.\n> \n> The class audit also closes layer path/key metadata, unowned filenames and decoded native identities before deletion and in final descriptor accounting. The [location-by-location audit](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/5019dade6d6f23e3017d141228461a1810ac9d4d/docs/validation/pr150-erasure-review-repair.md) covers journals, receipts, logs, metadata, refs, pack indexes/members, native payloads and bundle headers/body. Ten behavioral reversion groups fail and restored selections pass, including a writer-produced nonce compatibility control and the original directory-race refusal.\n> \n> Final-source focused results: broad erasure/accountability/fragment repairs **146/146**; decoder and composition c8 cohort **57/57** (JSON decoder and representation inspector each 100% in all four dimensions); packed power loss **5,546 native boundaries / 474 distinct crash images**, each replayed twice; lifecycle focus **42/42** across 35 selected native cuts; Node 22 **46/46**, including bounded 32 MiB streaming; complete fragments **56/56**. Static/privacy/changelog and committed self-host checks pass. Earlier failed and cancelled diagnostics are documented and excluded from passing counts. No installer retries.\n> \n> [Exact-head CI](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/41239154226) is pending. Full default npm/Bun matrices and fresh independent Codex review remain required. The issue stays open for orchestrator verification; no merge or release is performed.\n> \n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-31T22:27:17Z)\n>\n> The decoded-state repair is in [ccc49428c9487c94fc4b1841605e510f40ad0cfb](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/commit/ccc49428c9487c94fc4b1841605e510f40ad0cfb), supplementing the retained native ownership/recovery and physical-copy fixes.\n> \n> The re-review of 6dfc776 reproduced success while a quoted payload remained recoverable from an escaped destruction path. Raw serialized text was insufficient. The repair uses one bounded incremental JSON string decoder for materialized and streaming inspection, including keys, all escapes and UTF-16 pairs. Hex/base64/framing/compression compose under existing bounds, and recoverable prefixes are inspected even when a new codec guess later errors. Existing declared raw/base64 refusals, strict journal classification and physical-copy recovery remain.\n> \n> The class audit also closes layer path/key metadata, unowned filenames and decoded native identities before deletion and in final descriptor accounting. The [location-by-location audit](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/ccc49428c9487c94fc4b1841605e510f40ad0cfb/docs/validation/pr150-erasure-review-repair.md) covers journals, receipts, logs, metadata, refs, pack indexes/members, native payloads, native URLs and bundle headers/body. The final native-decoder audit also reproduced percent-escaped payload retention in file remotes on `5019dad`; bounded URL inspection now closes it in both scanners, with native remote-writer and loose/packed/composite regressions. Eighteen behavioral reversion groups fail and restored selections pass, including a writer-produced nonce compatibility control and the original directory-race refusal.\n> \n> Final-source focused results: broad erasure/accountability/fragment repairs **166/166**; decoder and composition c8 cohort **77/77** (JSON/URL decoders and representation inspector each 100% in all four dimensions); packed power loss **5,546 native boundaries / 474 distinct crash images**, each replayed twice; lifecycle focus **42/42** across 35 selected native cuts; Node 22 **66/66**, including bounded 32 MiB streaming; complete fragments **56/56** and packs **38/38**. Static/privacy/changelog and committed self-host checks pass. Earlier failed and cancelled diagnostics are documented and excluded from passing counts. No installer retries.\n> \n> [Exact-head CI](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/41248067260) is pending. Full default npm/Bun matrices and fresh independent Codex review remain required. The issue stays open for orchestrator verification; no merge or release is performed.\n> \n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-01T02:58:20Z)\n>\n> Repair commit: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/commit/401c1be92abec082e633439a37471b6d9161fa5e\n> \n> The native recovery/process-marker and physical-copy fixes remain retained. This repair follows the requested provenance contract: native composition identities close split manifests and all contributing fragments; source edges cover unpublished FileId writes and working outputs before bytes; ordinary and signed local exports carry their actual input inventories; legacy operation summaries are structurally redacted, and repository log producers share the store lease through erasure completion. Unknown destruction/control artifacts, shared ownership, physical-copy plans and replacement fences retain their refusals.\n> \n> The receipt certifies native derivation of the listed object identities within owned storage. User-authored alternate encodings, independent names/metadata, caller-owned exports and external copies have explicit exclusions. The secondary raw/native-JSON audit is bounded to 16 MiB/eight levels and reports residue/limits without gating benign data.\n> \n> Evidence: broad cohort 228/228; targeted c8 73/73 with all four coverage dimensions at 100% per targeted file; packs 38/38; fragments 56/56; lifecycle selection 43/43 (18/800 and 18/988 cuts; full model remains CI); CLI 2/2; Node 22 18/18; native Bun 5/5. Packed power loss covers 6007 boundaries and 518 distinct complete crash images, each with two convergent replays. Fourteen distinct mutants fail and every restored control passes. Static/privacy/changelog checks, committed-head self-host acceptance and isolated identity audit pass. No installer timeout was retried.\n> \n> [Guarantee, class audit, exact commands and revert proofs](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/401c1be92abec082e633439a37471b6d9161fa5e/docs/validation/pr150-erasure-review-repair.md). [PM proof record](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/401c1be92abec082e633439a37471b6d9161fa5e/.agents/pm/features/pm-vcs-phase6packs.toon).\n> \n> [CI](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/41266968691), [CodeQL](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/41266968686), [dependency automation](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/41266968684). Snapshot: windows-acceptance-launcher (26) success; test (26) in_progress; test (22) in_progress; windows-acceptance-launcher (22) success; codeql success; dependency auto-merge skipped (non-Dependabot PR). The full matrix is not awaited.\n> \n> The issue remains open for orchestrator verification. No review threads were replied to or resolved; no merge or release was performed.\n> \n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-01T06:32:50Z)\n>\n> Fixed the fourth review's three reproduced provenance gaps in `8ee69ad3611a356e1483309e599b3847e9aaece1` (PR #150).\n> \n> - Merge/replay and the remaining native derivation sites now certify input object identities before publishing bytes. Erasure follows those edges transitively and retires derived worktree outputs only with current birth/content ownership evidence.\n> - Legacy payloads without certificates remain readable/exportable, but erasure refuses with typed `uncatalogued_provenance` and names the unknown objects before deletion. The regression writes the exact `ccc4942` conflict-side frame; rewriting the same address cannot manufacture provenance.\n> - Composition inspection memoizes distinct objects, checks deadline and pinned lease inside traversal, and enforces bounded logical/cache/edge work. The eight-object 512 TiB fixture refuses after one root read within its time bound.\n> \n> Evidence: [derivation inventory and revert controls](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/8ee69ad3611a356e1483309e599b3847e9aaece1/docs/validation/pr150-erasure-review-repair.md). Disposable mutations produced 27 expected failures across 21 groups, followed by 27 restored passes. Local provenance 97/97; accountability/fragments/storage 218/218; lifecycle 43/43 with 18 sampled cuts per scenario; packs 38/38; composition/replay 32/32; publication 8/8; packed durability 1/1 covering 6,225 native boundaries and 538 distinct crash images, each replayed twice. Node 22 selection 10/10 and Bun provenance 31/31. Static, privacy, changelog, committed-HEAD self-host and identity checks pass. Coverage thresholds and existing ownership/destruction/physical-copy guards remain unchanged. Full release CI and independent re-review remain pending; leaving this issue open for orchestrator verification.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-01T07:36:20Z)\n>\n> Fixed the fifth review's two GC/provenance blockers in `34c35681ca720a89b01c66585edcfd2bbc2d33ac` (PR #150).\n> \n> Certificates now retain the complete deduplicated transitive input set, including native manifest pages/fragments, plus explicit unknown ancestry. GC preserves these metadata records and upgrades old direct-parent records before collection; preview shares the proof without persisting. Erasure checks present payloads and registered native outputs, so a missing old ancestor or input certificate produces typed `uncatalogued_provenance` before deletion, naming derived identities. Registered output cleanup no longer depends on an intermediate manifest still existing. Ordinary old reads and exports remain supported.\n> \n> [Class audit, guarantee and revert evidence](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/34c35681ca720a89b01c66585edcfd2bbc2d33ac/docs/validation/pr150-erasure-review-repair.md): 8 disposable mutation groups, 12 expected behavioral failures and 12 restored passes. This includes the old catalog-presence-only decision, both collected legacy merges, collected new/old manifest outputs, GC-anywhere histories and the corrected large-blob test.\n> \n> Local gates pass: final-source provenance 45/45 with both proof modules at 100% in all four coverage dimensions; combined provenance/erasure 108/108 plus targeted 5/5; broader accountability/storage/GC/packs/fragments/legacy fetch 341/341; lifecycle 43/43 sampling 18/818 and 18/1006 cuts; packed power loss 1/1 across 6,225 boundaries and 538 distinct crash images, each replayed twice; Bun 45/45; Node 22 focused 12/12. Static, privacy and changelog checks pass. The committed archive and commit identity are verified at HEAD. An interrupted unfiltered PM run is excluded from these counts. No installer timeout was retried.\n> \n> Full release CI, the complete lifecycle matrices and independent re-review remain pending. Existing ownership, destruction-classification and physical-copy guards remain intact. Leaving this issue open for orchestrator verification.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-01T14:54:29Z)\n>\n> Follow-up repair in [6a0d4b5](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/commit/6a0d4b5d6253a1e2639c8af78fec34dff0fb557a). The prior native control/storage classification and all-location deletion plan remain intact. The sixth-review leak came from retaining a manifest container's inputs without retaining its equivalent whole-blob identity. Certificates now record whole identities, members and transitive roots before payload publication; GC retains that evidence. Erasure follows equivalent representations and their descendants even after an intermediate is collected. Canonical record/link/conflict payloads use the same literal-byte identity route. Unknown ancestry still refuses before deletion.\n> \n> Evidence: exact loose/packed collected-manifest cases, four equivalence-through-GC histories, late whole arrival and six typed-equivalence cases fail under isolated behavioral reverts and pass after restoration. The complete packed power-loss gate passes 6247 native boundaries / 538 distinct crash images / two convergent engine replays per image. Complete pack/GC passes 70/70; fragments/pages 97/97; Bun provenance 66/66; Node 22 selection 15/15. All 17 touched production modules measure 100% in all four coverage dimensions. Committed-head self-host acceptance passes.\n> \n> [Validation and guarantee](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/6a0d4b5d6253a1e2639c8af78fec34dff0fb557a/docs/validation/pr150-erasure-review-repair.md). Fresh [CI](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/41318289087) is queued; full CI and independent re-review remain pending. Issue remains open for orchestrator verification.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-01T17:26:32Z)\n>\n> The seventh-review erasure gaps are fixed in 56b241ac0255cb8ea506100a7e04cf3df2a780d8.\n> \n> Descriptor certification previously read from offset zero while fixed/CDC publication consumed the caller cursor. Both now use one explicit positional range; checksum-bound private blocks ensure the bytes certified are the bytes stored. Input snapshots close the same class in ordinary writes, arrivals, local exports and worktree output. Accountability previously checked directories before its final reopens; it now checks them afterwards and requires two matching complete passes, refusing bounded non-convergence and retaining pending cleanup.\n> \n> Revert evidence: all nine advanced-descriptor/GC regressions fail with the descriptor fix reverted and pass restored; loose and packed reopen regressions fail for both first-pass and second-pass barrier reversions and pass restored; both convergence controls are sensitive. All 28 new behavioral controls pass after restoration. The packed power-loss matrix passed 6,247 boundaries / 538 distinct crash images with two convergent replays each. Node 22 and 26 each pass the 46-case final regression selection; native Bun passes 75 provenance and six reopen/convergence cases. All five touched modules measure 100% statements, branches, functions and lines. Static, privacy, changelog, committed-HEAD self-host and isolated identity checks pass.\n> \n> The complete class audit, concurrency scope and revert ledger are in [the seventh-review validation record](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/56b241ac0255cb8ea506100a7e04cf3df2a780d8/docs/validation/pr150-seventh-review.md). Full release CI and independent re-review remain pending. The issue remains open for orchestrator verification."
